18. (This question is worth 14 points)

Given the function f(x) = cos^2(ωx) + √3 sin(ωx) cos(ωx) + m  (ω > 0, m ∈ R). From the three conditions (Condition 1), (Condition 2), (Condition 3) choose two that can determine the analytic expression of f(x) as the known information.

(I) Find the analytic expression of f(x) and its minimum value;

(II) If the function f(x) has exactly one zero in the interval [0, t] (t > 0), find the range of t.

Condition 1: The least positive period of f(x) is π;

Condition 2: The graph of f(x) passes through the point (0, 1/2);

Condition 3: The maximum value of f(x) is 3/2.

Note: If the chosen conditions do not meet the requirements, 0 points will be given; if multiple sets of conditions satisfy the requirements and are solved separately, scoring will be based on the first set solved.

